# Test Instance Data Block: DOL_Starter_Test_Instance

## Data Block Overview
This instance data block provides the memory and interface for the DOL_Starter_Test function block.

## Instance Declaration
```scl
// In your main program or test organization block:
VAR
    // DOL Starter Test Instance
    FB_DOL_Starter_Test : FB DOL_Starter_Test;
END_VAR
```

## Memory Map
| Variable | Offset | Type | Description |
|----------|--------|------|-------------|
| **Inputs** | | | |
| bTest_Mode_Enable | +0 | BOOL | Enable test mode |
| bTest_Start_PB | +0.1 | BOOL | Test start button simulation |
| bTest_Stop_PB | +0.2 | BOOL | Test stop button simulation |
| bTest_Overload | +0.3 | BOOL | Test overload simulation |
| bTest_Contactor_FB | +0.4 | BOOL | Test contactor feedback simulation |
| bManual_Contactor_Test | +0.5 | BOOL | Manual contactor test |
| bReset_Test | +0.6 | BOOL | Reset test results |
| **Outputs** | | | |
| bSim_Start_PB | +2.0 | BOOL | Simulated start to DOL starter |
| bSim_Stop_PB | +2.1 | BOOL | Simulated stop to DOL starter |
| bSim_Overload | +2.2 | BOOL | Simulated overload to DOL starter |
| bSim_Aux_Contact | +2.3 | BOOL | Simulated aux contact to DOL starter |
| bTest_Mode_Active | +2.4 | BOOL | Test mode indicator |
| bTest_Contactor_Out | +2.5 | BOOL | Manual test contactor output |
| bRunning_Verified | +2.6 | BOOL | Running status verified |
| bFault_Verified | +2.7 | BOOL | Fault status verified |
| bReady_Verified | +2.8 | BOOL | Ready status verified |
| bTest_Success | +2.9 | BOOL | Test passed indication |
| bTest_Fail | +2.10 | BOOL | Test failed indication |
| **IN_OUT Variables** | | | |
| bDOL_Contactor | +4.0 | BOOL | DOL starter contactor output |
| bDOL_Running_Ind | +4.1 | BOOL | DOL starter running indicator |
| bDOL_Fault_Ind | +4.2 | BOOL | DOL starter fault indicator |
| bDOL_Ready_Ind | +4.3 | BOOL | DOL starter ready indicator |
| **Static Variables** | | | |
| bTest_Result_Latch | +6.0 | BOOL | Test result latch |
| bStart_Test_Pass | +6.1 | BOOL | Start test pass flag |
| bStop_Test_Pass | +6.2 | BOOL | Stop test pass flag |
| bOverload_Test_Pass | +6.3 | BOOL | Overload test pass flag |
| bFeedback_Test_Pass | +6.4 | BOOL | Feedback test pass flag |
| iTest_Counter | +8 | INT | Test counter |
| tTest_Delay | +10.0 | TON | Test delay timer |

## Total Memory Requirements
- Input variables: 1 byte
- Output variables: 2 bytes
- IN_OUT variables: 1 byte
- Static variables: 14 bytes
- **Total: 18 bytes**

## Usage Example
```scl
// In Test OB or Main OB:
// Connect test inputs
FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bTest_Mode_Enable := %I4.4;     // Test mode enable
FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bTest_Start_PB := %I4.0;        // Test start PB
FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bTest_Stop_PB := %I4.1;         // Test stop PB
FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bTest_Overload := %I4.2;        // Test overload
FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bTest_Contactor_FB := %I4.3;    // Test contactor FB
FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bManual_Contactor_Test := %I4.5; // Manual test
FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bReset_Test := %I4.6;            // Reset test

// Connect to DOL starter outputs
FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bDOL_Contactor := FB_DOL_Starter_1.bContactor;
FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bDOL_Running_Ind := FB_DOL_Starter_1.bRunning_Ind;
FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bDOL_Fault_Ind := FB_DOL_Starter_1.bFault_Ind;
FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bDOL_Ready_Ind := FB_DOL_Starter_1.bReady_Ind;

// Call the test function block
FB_DOL_Starter_Test();

// Connect simulated outputs to DOL starter inputs
FB_DOL_Starter_1.bStart_PB := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bSim_Start_PB;
FB_DOL_Starter_1.bStop_PB := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bSim_Stop_PB;
FB_DOL_Starter_1.bOverload := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bSim_Overload;
FB_DOL_Starter_1.bAux_Contact := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bSim_Aux_Contact;

// Connect test outputs
%Q4.0 := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bSim_Start_PB;        // Simulated start
%Q4.1 := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bSim_Stop_PB;         // Simulated stop
%Q4.2 := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bSim_Overload;       // Simulated overload
%Q4.3 := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bSim_Aux_Contact;    // Simulated aux contact
%Q4.4 := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bTest_Mode_Active;   // Test mode indicator
%Q4.5 := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bTest_Contactor_Out; // Manual test output

%Q5.0 := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bRunning_Verified;   // Running verified
%Q5.1 := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bFault_Verified;     // Fault verified
%Q5.2 := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bReady_Verified;     // Ready verified
%Q5.3 := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bTest_Success;       // Test success
%Q5.4 := FB_DOL_Starter_Test.bTest_Fail;          // Test fail
```

## TIA Portal Test Implementation Steps

### 1. Create Test Function Block
1. Open TIA Portal Project4
2. Navigate to PLC → Program blocks
3. Right-click → Add new block
4. Select "Function block (FB)"
5. Name: `DOL_Starter_Test`
6. Number: FB2 (or next available)
7. Language: SCL
8. Copy the SCL code from `dol_starter_test.fb`

### 2. Create Test Instance Data Block
1. Right-click on Function blocks → Add new block
2. Select "Data block (DB)"
3. Name: `DOL_Starter_Test_Instance`
4. Type: `FB DOL_Starter_Test`
5. Number: DB2 (or next available)

### 3. Configure Test Hardware I/O
1. Open Hardware configuration
2. Assign test digital inputs:
   - %I4.0: Test start button
   - %I4.1: Test stop button
   - %I4.2: Test overload simulation
   - %I4.3: Test contactor feedback
   - %I4.4: Test mode enable
   - %I4.5: Manual contactor test
   - %I4.6: Reset test
3. Assign test digital outputs:
   - %Q4.0-%Q4.5: Simulated signals and indicators
   - %Q5.0-%Q5.4: Test verification outputs

### 4. Integrate Test with DOL Starter
1. Open Main OB (OB1) or create test OB
2. Add both function block calls
3. Connect test FB to DOL starter FB as shown in usage example
4. Ensure proper signal flow between blocks

### 5. Test Configuration
1. Compile the project
2. Download to PLCSIM for testing
3. Enable test mode
4. Execute individual test procedures
5. Monitor test verification outputs
6. Document test results

## Test Mode Operation

### Normal Operation (Test Mode Disabled)
- Test signals pass through to DOL starter
- Simulated outputs disabled
- Manual test outputs disabled
- DOL starter operates normally with real I/O

### Test Mode (Test Mode Enabled)
- Real I/O disconnected from DOL starter
- Test simulation signals active
- Automated test sequences available
- Manual testing capabilities enabled
- Verification outputs monitor DOL starter behavior

## Test Scenarios

### Scenario 1: Automated Start Test
1. Enable test mode
2. Press test start button
3. Monitor test success/fail outputs
4. Verify running indicator activates
5. Reset test for next scenario

### Scenario 2: Automated Stop Test
1. Enable test mode
2. Start motor using test start
3. Press test stop button
4. Monitor test success/fail outputs
5. Verify ready indicator activates
6. Reset test for next scenario

### Scenario 3: Manual Testing
1. Enable test mode
2. Use manual test inputs
3. Manually verify each function
4. Document results
5. Reset test when complete

## Safety During Testing
- Test mode should have physical lockout
- Emergency stop must remain functional
- Ensure equipment is isolated during testing
- Use test mode only in controlled environments
- Never bypass safety interlocks for testing

## Test Data Logging
The test function block includes:
- Test counter for tracking test executions
- Individual test pass/fail flags
- Overall test result latching
- Verification status outputs

These can be logged to a data block for traceability and quality control.

## Integration with Quality Systems
Test results can be:
- Exported to quality management system
- Used for production acceptance
- Tracked for maintenance scheduling
- Documented for regulatory compliance
- Used for continuous improvement
